x86_64-linux  clang zeroes the `Wide<5,6>` and the empty `List` temporaries with a call to memset where cxx1 writes nothing for a class with no members - the difference S-09 recorded in CLAUDE.md, a question about emission and not about a name; the other 20 names agree.
x86_64-windows  the same memset; every other name agrees. arm64-darwin agrees on all 20.
arm64-darwin  a definition cxx1 emits and clang emits only for a use - an inline function or special member (C1/D1 beside C2/D2), a template instance, an unused internal constant or exit helper: emission, not spelling (docs/CLAUDE-history.md, "Weak definitions, and the link that follows from them"; tests/open/names-register.txt, "Emission, not names"); and clang 19 spells a non-type parameter of dependent type TnT_/TpTn, which cxx1, cl and earlier clangs do not (tests/open/names-register.txt, "Clang 19, not cxx1") - 12 names, e.g. <__Z13bracedPatternIJEEiv >__Z13bracedPatternITpTniJEEiv (r6n, names.sh on the Windows box beside clang 19.1.5, 2026-11-15)
